WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:05.780
- Now, when the police raided your place

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.430
the five people

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.773
they found in your freezer,
(suspenseful music)

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.983
did you cut them up too?

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.650
- God, that was a long time ago.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.283
- People don't change.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.268
I should know, my mom sent
me to gay conversion camp.

00:00:27.268 --> 00:00:30.080
(laughs)

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.123
Amazing, that you ended up in minimum.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.823
The Russian mob must've sprung
for one hell of a lawyer.

00:00:42.597 --> 00:00:44.767
- You don't know a thing about me.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:48.767
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.600
- I come here to buy a boat,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.785
not become some god damn pirate!

00:00:55.785 --> 00:00:58.035
(laughing)

00:01:01.677 --> 00:01:05.713
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:07.986
- Please don't drop them.

00:01:07.986 --> 00:01:10.069
- Out there, shake hands.

00:01:12.827 --> 00:01:16.827
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:19.735 --> 00:01:22.402
- This is very important people.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.857
- Go meet his wife.

00:01:35.857 --> 00:01:36.780
- I've been cooking all day.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.447
I smell like onions.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:42.133
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:45.097
- I have someone to make you acquaintance.

00:01:55.462 --> 00:01:57.840
- The third time, the same thing happened.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.480
And the farmer looks at his wife,

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.960
then back at the penguin

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.683
and finally the penguin goes,

00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:06.350
(laughs)

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.810
he's not an eggplant man,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.552
he is retarded.

00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:12.635
(laughs)

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.470
You get it, 'cause he--

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:16.303
- We get it.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.883
- My brother was retarded.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.140
- I'm so sorry to hear that.

00:02:25.595 --> 00:02:27.940
You know my husband's a little slow.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.180
Says he was dropped on
his head when he was born,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.230
just my luck, they couldn't have dropped

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.700
him on his dick?
(laughing)

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.050
- I think I slept wrong last night.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.176
Should we call it a
short walk today ladies?

00:02:39.176 --> 00:02:40.009
- Yeah.

00:02:40.009 --> 00:02:41.960
- Awe, you barely broke a sweat.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.540
- My son has dentist appointment.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.740
- Oh, Okay.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.040
- We're close to your house, no?

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.060
- Yeah, right over there.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.410
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.460
- We'll let you know.

00:02:53.897 --> 00:02:56.897
(light piano music)

00:03:02.492 --> 00:03:05.659
(Russian style music)

00:03:07.997 --> 00:03:10.830
(traffic honking)

00:03:55.627 --> 00:03:56.460
- Oh no.

00:03:59.166 --> 00:04:02.766
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:02.766 --> 00:04:03.599
- Red.

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:04.500
- And the penguin goes.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.470
He's not an eggplant, he's retarded.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.220
It's fucking funny!

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.053
- Is just not.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:12.343
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:12.343 --> 00:04:14.055
on your head make me giggle though.

00:04:14.055 --> 00:04:14.967
(laughing)

00:04:14.967 --> 00:04:16.302
(intense music)
- You.

00:04:16.302 --> 00:04:19.263
(all gasp)

00:04:19.263 --> 00:04:22.730
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.236
- Oh shit.

00:04:24.236 --> 00:04:26.340
- What the fuck were you thinking?

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.670
After all Ganya's done for us?

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:29.567
He love those tits!

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:30.710
- He can get them back!

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.520
There's plenty more of
them at the tit store.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.890
- Did you count to ten?

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.660
You supposed to count to ten!

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:36.905
- I never even wanted to speak to those

00:04:36.905 --> 00:04:38.900
(word in Russian), you made me!

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.650
- Why did you do such a thing?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.530
- Because they left me out!

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.450
Because they made fun of me!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.480
Because no matter how hard you try,

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.640
and how much we want it,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.523
there's the people who serve the bread

00:04:49.523 --> 00:04:52.110
and people who eat the bread,

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.280
and for once it would be nice

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.438
if you would be on my side!

00:04:55.438 --> 00:04:57.521
(crying)

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:07.420
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.393
- How bad?

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.363
- They want $60,000.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.810
- No boob job costs $60,000,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.900
that's crazy.
(crying)

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:27.923
- This one does.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.673
- I was, I was just,

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.530
they're so mean!

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.213
- So are the men they married.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.567
They meaner.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.877
- I'm sorry dear.

00:05:51.737 --> 00:05:53.253
- Figure out something,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:56.953
we always do.

00:06:02.311 --> 00:06:04.090
(doorbell rings)

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.923
- Hello?

00:06:07.763 --> 00:06:10.680
(subway whistling)

00:06:20.692 --> 00:06:24.609
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:31.036 --> 00:06:32.036
- It's fine.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.310
It will make things right for us.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.372
- This doesn't feel right.

00:06:37.372 --> 00:06:40.687
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:40.687 --> 00:06:42.164
- We're fine.

00:06:42.164 --> 00:06:43.884
Work it out.

00:06:43.884 --> 00:06:47.232
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:47.232 --> 00:06:52.232
(door slams)
(whistle blows)

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:57.063
(speaking in foreign language)

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.420
- It's not about the prices.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.873
It's about the books.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.540
- We have to move product regularly,

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.820
then and only then, we
can explain other income.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.773
- Maybe you're not thinking big enough.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.223
Restaurants come and go, yes?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.410
Look at this place, every
week we almost close.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.388
But not schools, not hospitals,

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.620
- Galya-
- All I'm saying is,

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.760
you get something big, something steady,

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.420
like the Italians have with the garbage,

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.100
then you're not out chasing bids.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:50.150
My father, he sold candy.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.270
Out of a box, everyday,
up and down the street.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.030
He walked so much he
wore holes in his shoes.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.460
Until one day, he passed by an army base,

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.970
right after the soldier's lunch time,

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.780
and he realized that all he had to do

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:06.350
was stand there and open his box.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:10.530
He sold out in minutes,
so he did it again.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.130
Day after day.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.970
There were always soldiers,

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.213
there was always lunch, and
they always wanted candy bars.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.873
No more holes in his shoes.

00:08:24.546 --> 00:08:28.463
(speaking in foreign language)

00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:35.458
(laughing)

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.580
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:22.655 --> 00:09:25.310
- Anyway, our guy looked into the

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:28.730
government contracts
thing, schools, hospitals.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.740
- Yeah?

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.897
- Looks like we'll be able
to work something out.

00:09:39.305 --> 00:09:43.222
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:49.469 --> 00:09:51.484
- And now I complain to you.

00:09:51.484 --> 00:09:55.401
(speaking in foreign language)

00:10:08.845 --> 00:10:10.030
- We can discuss that another day.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.430
- I spoke to Olga again, she says these

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.060
retirement communities are only going

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.700
to keep popping up, if we
get in at the beginning.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.450
- Sure, sure, next time
(speaking in foreign language).

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.790
- They can't wait five minutes?

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.090
I'm offering a gold mine here.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.570
And it's not even illegal.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.660
- They'll get excited
when they finally hear it.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:37.230
- Every time they forget I'm
the one with the good ideas.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.400
The prison contract?

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:43.033
That was me.
(speaking in foreign language)

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.720
So, meeting with the Serb.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.703
You ready for that?

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.940
(Sighs)

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.430
- You think it's too late
to marry Sonja Chekova?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.320
My mother thinks her dad

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.400
could get me into courses
at the gem society.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:11.210
- You don't want to be a
diamond cutter at Zales.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.810
And you don't want to live
next door to your mother.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.283
That's the only reason mother
is nice to that stupid girl.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.290
You can do better than Sonja Chekova

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.253
With her underbite.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.763
- Last time we went out, the
guy didn't die all the way.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:32.710
Vlad had to finish him with a tire iron.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.130
- I don't want to know about these things.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.763
- His eye popped out of
his head like a slinky toy.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.620
- Maybe they have
another job you could do?

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:41.453
I could ask.

00:11:41.453 --> 00:11:42.750
- No, I'm fine, I can handle it,

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:44.383
I don't know why I'm complaining.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.393
- Good things come to those who stay late.

00:11:52.234 --> 00:11:54.119
(car horn honks)

00:11:54.119 --> 00:11:54.952
- Ah, that's me.

00:11:54.952 --> 00:11:55.920
- Oh, your mother can wait!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:56.753
Have you cookie!

00:11:56.753 --> 00:11:58.700
- She'll yell at me, it's not worth it.

00:12:02.562 --> 00:12:03.395
- Good night.

00:12:05.434 --> 00:12:08.851
(melancholy piano music)

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.997
(speaking in foreign language)

00:12:24.134 --> 00:12:27.261
- Are you ever going to let me speak?

00:12:27.261 --> 00:12:31.178
(speaking in foreign language)

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:39.080
- I might as well wait in the
freezer while the men talk.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:42.323
If you don't want me to speak
up when I notice mistakes.

00:12:53.501 --> 00:12:57.418
(speaking in foreign language)

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.139
- Keep him on look out,
have him run errands.

00:13:10.139 --> 00:13:14.056
(speaking in foreign language)

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:17.040
- Get Donila or Constantine.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.290
they're able to prove themselves.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.793
That aren't such mama's boys.

00:13:21.768 --> 00:13:24.413
(speaking in foreign language)

00:13:24.413 --> 00:13:27.923
- (Sighs) I'm a mama, I know mama's boys.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:34.263
The boys are at Uleyla's,
we could go out to dinner?

00:13:34.263 --> 00:13:36.191
- What about Who Wants
To Be A Millionaire?

00:13:36.191 --> 00:13:37.900
Don't you want to see
that college student win?

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.360
- What does he need a million dollars for?

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:43.060
They always think they
know, and guess and poof!

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:44.373
They never walk away.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.073
- Not everyone is smart as my Galina.

00:13:51.921 --> 00:13:54.588
(doors banging)

00:13:56.865 --> 00:14:00.782
(speaking in foreign language)

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.782
- Inspectors come unannounced.

00:14:06.782 --> 00:14:10.699
(speaking in foreign language)

00:14:21.532 --> 00:14:24.615
(sad downbeat music)

00:14:28.748 --> 00:14:29.581
- Gali?

00:14:51.174 --> 00:14:53.257
(gasps)

